  "body": "What happens: on main, `OpParams::stamp_with` for `OpParams::WireContour` (`crates/app/src/operation/params.rs`, the `// The wire contour (#532)` arm) writes the side as `u8::from(p.side == WireSide::Punch)` and never writes `clearance`. Since #1109 the side has four values (Die, Punch, Left, Right), so Die, Left and Right digest the same byte, and an edit of the run-out clearance moves nothing. An open run edited from Left to Right (or a new clearance) keeps the same stamp, so its generated path is not read as stale: the post goes out with the old path, whose kerf is on the side the user no longer states (the wire laws still judge the kerf against the part, so a gouge into the part is caught, but the program no longer matches the operation).\n\nExpected: every stored word moves the stamp (the arm's own comment). Write the side as its own discriminant, and the clearance (only when the side is Left/Right, or only when it differs from the default, so a closed cut's stamp stays what it was).\n\nEvidence: found while refreshing PR #1163 (#536, wire taper), which adds `taper_deg` to the same arm the same way. Not changed there: it's out of that PR's scope.\n\nDone means: a pinning test shows that editing a Wire Contour's side Left -> Right, or its clearance, changes `current_stamp` and marks the generated path stale. Also, a closed die/punch cut's stamp is unchanged from before.\n",
